<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1.0/policyconfig.dtd">

<!--
  docs/design.md §3: the studio is never root. It reads with the same two libraries the
  CLI reads with — everything it reads is world readable, so looking needs no
  privilege at all — and every write it does is `pkexec omahouse <verb>`, which
  is the CLI, with the same checks and the same refusals.

  So there is one action here and not one per verb. What is being authorised is
  "run omahouse as root", and the verbs behind it are the writing half of
  docs/design.md §7: profile add, remove, enforce, default, allow, deny, limit, grant.
  The reading half needs none of this and must never be behind it — the
  fiscalised user runs `omahouse status` to see what is left of their own day,
  and a prompt for an administrator's password to read your own balance is a
  product nobody uses twice.

  `auth_admin` and not `auth_admin_keep`: the operator of docs/design.md §1 is whoever
  is in wheel, and the thing being changed is somebody else's evening. A five
  minute window where the machine will do it again without asking is a window
  where the person it is about is standing at the same keyboard.

  `auth_admin` and not `auth_self`, which would be a shorter file and a hole.
  This action is the only gate in front of the CLI running as root -- omahouse
  does not refuse a write from an account that is under rules, because by then
  it is root and there is nobody left to refuse -- so `auth_self` here is the
  fiscalised account authorising its own release with its own password.

  What `auth_admin` cannot say is *which* administrator, and on a machine with
  two people in wheel the prompt takes the other one's password without saying
  so. That is said in `org.omarchy.omahouse.rules`, beside this file: an
  administrator authenticates as themselves, and everybody else arrives here
  and is asked for an administrator's password exactly as written above.
-->
<policyconfig>

  <vendor>omarchy</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://omarchy.org</vendor_url>
  <icon_name>omahouse</icon_name>

  <action id="org.omarchy.omahouse.manage">
    <description>Change the house rules</description>
    <description xml:lang="pt_BR">Mudar as regras da casa</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to change which programs an account may run, and for how long.</message>
    <message xml:lang="pt_BR">É preciso autenticar para mudar quais programas uma conta pode abrir, e por quanto tempo.</message>

    <defaults>
      <allow_any>auth_admin</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>auth_admin</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin</allow_active>
    </defaults>

    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/bin/omahouse</annotate>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.allow_gui">true</annotate>
  </action>

</policyconfig>
